{"uid": "mfg-1914-10-04", "question_type": "counterfactual", "question_subtype": "remove_order", "raw_text": "Based on my analysis of the Plant 1914, Period 10 data:\n\n**Day 134 ledger for ATN01K24P:**\n- End of day 133 stock: 18905\n- Produced: 4500\n- Ordered/shipped: 3406\n- End of day 134 stock: 19999\n\n**If the day 134 order (3406 units) had not been placed:**\n- End of day 134 stock would be: 18905 + 4500 - 0 = 23405\n\n**Day 135 ledger:**\n- Produced: 4000, Ordered/shipped: 2461\n- Without the day 134 order, end of day 135 stock: 23405 + 4000 - 2461 = 24944\n- Recorded stock is 21538, so 24944 > 21538 \u2192 Choice 3 is **true**\n\n**Day 136 ledger:**\n- Produced: 5000, Ordered/shipped: 3112\n- Without the day 134 order, end of day 136 stock: 24944 + 5000 - 3112 = 26832\n- Recorded stock is 23426, so 26832 > 23426 \u2192 Choice 1 is **true**\n\n**Choice 0 (ATWWP001K24P on day 135):**\nATWWP001K24P has 0 stock at end of day 134 and 0 production on day 135, so the order cannot ship regardless of capacity. Choice 0 is **false**.\n\n**Choice 2 (MAR01K24P on day 138):**\nIn the recorded scenario, the MAR01K24P order on day 138 already shipped in full (1072 units shipped from 4325 stock). Since ATWWP001K24P and SE200G24P have 0 stock on day 134 (when ATN01K24P would free capacity), no other products benefit from freed capacity on day 134. MAR01K24P had no backorders and had ample stock, so it still ships in full. But this is not a *change* caused by removing the ATN01K24P order\u2014it was already happening. The question asks what \"would have happened\" as a consequence, and since MAR01K24P ships in full in both scenarios, this is not a causal consequence. Choice 2 is **false**.\n\n{\"choices\": {\"0\": false, \"1\": true, \"2\": false, \"3\": true}}", "parsed": {"choices": {"0": false, "1": true, "2": false, "3": true}}, "score": {"question_correct": false, "options_correct": 3, "options_total": 4}, "usage": {"input_tokens": 219363, "cached_input_tokens": 0, "o